cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Quantum Noise Profiler: provenance-aware, sequentially calibrated qubit noise monitoring"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below, and cite the frameworks it builds on (Qiskit, Qiskit Aer, Qiskit Experiments, Cirq)."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Woodyard"
    given-names: "Christopher"
    affiliation: "Vers3Dynamics"
version: "0.3.0.dev0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/topherchris420/quantum-noise-profiler"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - noise characterization
  - drift detection
  - sequential testing
  - e-values
  - anytime-valid inference
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A monitoring library that tracks per-qubit noise with explicit provenance
  (observed, inferred, measured), detects degradation with anytime-valid
  e-processes under an explicit session error budget, issues threshold-crossing
  forecasts with predictive intervals and machine-readable abstention reasons,
  applies absolute thresholds only to workload-independent readout probes, and
  refuses to report relaxation times when the single-exponential model is
  contradicted by the data or the measurement drifted during the sweep.
  Evaluated with preregistered simulation studies and a subsequent
  preregistered 14-job assumption-check pilot on IBM ibm_fez (October 2026).
  Six of ten probe series rejected a constant-rate binomial model across
  batches; zero of ten T1 sweeps detected within-job reference drift.
  Hardware warning accuracy and generality have not been established.
